0103 | \section{Introduction}
0104 | Let $X$ be a hyperbolic curve over a number field $K$. Then, by a theorem of Siegel in the case $X$ is affine \cite{siegel} and by Faltings \cite{faltings1983} in general, $X$ has only finitely many integral points. The Chabauty--Kim method seeks to give a new proof of finiteness, and a method for determining the set of points, using the tools of $p$-adic differential equations and reciprocity laws for Galois cohomology. Before explaining the Chabauty--Kim method more precisely, we clarify what we mean by integral points. Let $\overline{X}$ be a smooth projective curve over $K$, with $X\subset \overline{X}$ and complement $D:=\overline{X}-X$. We assume that $X$ is hyperbolic, i.e. that $2g(\overline{X})+\# D(\overline{K})>2$. Let $\mathcal{\overline{X}}$ be a regular model of $X$ over $\mathcal{O}_{K,S}$, for $S$ a finite set of primes, $\mathcal{D}\subset \mathcal{X}$ a normal crossings divisor, and $\mathcal{X}:=\overline{\mathcal{X}}-\mathcal{D}$. Then the theorems of Faltings and Siegel imply that $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_{K,S})$ is finite.
0105 | 
0106 | Let $p$ be a prime which splits completely in $K$, which is a prime of good reduction for $\mathcal{X}$ (in this paper, when we say that a rational prime is a prime of good reduction for $\mathcal{X}$, we will mean that for all $v|p$, $v$ is not in $S$, $\overline{X}$ has good reduction at $v$ and $\mathcal{D}$ is \'etale over $\mathcal{O}_v $). Then Kim's method produces nested subsets $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,n}$ of $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )=\prod _{v|p}\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_{K_v })$, each containing the $S$-integral points of $\mathcal{X}$:
0107 | \[
0108 | \mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )\supset \mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,1} \supset \mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,1} \supset \ldots \supset \mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_{K,S}).
0109 | \]
0110 | When $S$ is empty, these sets will be written simply as $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_n$, and in the case $X=\overline{X}$ is projective, they will be written simply as $X(K\otimes \Q _p )_n$.
0111 | A detailed description of $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,n} $ is given in section \ref{sec:unalb}.
0112 | 
0113 | When $K=\Q$, Kim conjectured that $\mathcal{X}(\mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,n}$ is finite for all $n\gg 0$. In \cite{kim:siegel}, Kim proved that $\mathcal{X}(\Z _p )_{S,n} $ is finite for all $n\gg 0$ when $\mathcal{X}=\mathbb{P}^1 -\{ 0,1, \infty \}$. In \cite{kim2010p}, Kim proved the eventual finiteness conjecture for $X=E-O$, where $E$ is an elliptic curve with complex multiplication. In \cite{kim:chabauty}, Kim showed that eventual finiteness for general $X/\Q $ is implied by the Bloch--Kato conjectures or the Jannsen conjectures. In \cite{coates2010selmer}, Coates and Kim proved eventual finiteness when $X/\Q $ is a curve whose Jacobian has complex multiplication. This was subsequently generalised by Ellenberg and Hast \cite{ellenberg2017rational} to prove finiteness of $X(\Q _p )_n$ when $X/\Q $ is a smooth projective geometrically irreducible curve admitting a surjective morphism $X_L \to Y$ to a curve $Y/L$ with CM Jacobian, where $L|\Q $ is a finite extension. This is then used to give a new proof of finiteness of $X(\Q )$ whenever $X$ is a solvable cover of $\mathbb{P}^1$.
0114 | 
0115 | \subsection{Main results}
0116 | The main results of this paper concern generalisations of Kim's theorems to the case $K$ is a number field. When $K$ is totally real, and $X=\mathbb{P}^1 -\{ 0,1,\infty \}$, and $S$ is any set of primes, finiteness of $X(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,n}$ for $n\gg 0$ was proved independently by Hadian \cite{hadian2011motivic} and Kim \cite{kim2012tangential}.
0117 | 
0118 | \begin{theorem}\label{finiteness}
0119 | \begin{enumerate}
0120 | Let $K$ be a number field, and $p$ a (rational) prime which splits completely in $K$.
0121 | \item Let $D\subset \mathbb{P}^1 _K$ be a closed subscheme with more than two $\overline{K}$-valued points, and define $X:=\mathbb{P}^1 -D$. Let  $S$ be a finite set of primes, and $\mathcal{X}/\mathcal{O}_{K,S}$ a model as above. Then, if $p$ is a prime of good reduction for $\mathcal{X}$, then $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p  )_{S,n} $ is finite for all $n\gg 0$.
0122 | \item Let $X/K$ be a smooth projective curve of genus $g>1$. Suppose $p$ is a prime of good reduction for $X/K$. Then the conjecture of Jannsen, or the conjecture of Bloch--Kato, implies that, for all primes $p$ of good reduction, $X(K\otimes \Q _p )_n $ is finite for all $n\gg 0$.
0123 | \item Let $X=E-O$,where $E/K$ is an elliptic curve with complex multiplication, and let $S$ a finite set of primes and $\mathcal{X}/ \mathcal{O}_{K,S}$ be as above. If $p$ is a prime of good reduction for $\mathcal{X}$, then $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_{S,n}$ is finite for all $n\gg 0$.
