0209 | \section{The intersection of $j_n (Z)$ with the Selmer variety}\label{sec:complete}
0210 | 
0211 | Given Proposition \ref{prop:useful_criterion}, to prove finiteness of $X(\mathcal{O}_K \otimes \mathbb{Z}_p )_n$, it is enough to prove that, for any positive-dimensional, geometrically irreducible smooth quasi-projective subvariety $Z\subset \Res (X)_{\overline{\Q }_p }$, and any virtual basepoint $b\in Z(\overline{Q }_p )\cap \Res (X)(\Q _p )$, there is a Galois-stable quotient $U$ of $U_n (\Res (X))$, such that
0212 | \begin{equation}\label{codim_inequality}
0213 | \codim _{U_n (Z/\Res (X))/F^0} (\loc _p (\Sel (U_N )_{\alpha })\cap U_n (Z/\Res (X))/F^0 )>\dim (Z).
0214 | \end{equation}
0215 | \subsection{Semi-simplicity properties of graded pieces of fundamental groups}
0216 | Let $n>0$, and let $X$ be a smooth projective curve of genus $g>1$ over $K$ with $n-1$ marked points $x_i \in X(K)$. Let $Y=X-\{x_1 ,\ldots ,x_{n-1}\}$. Let $\mathcal{M}_{g,n,K}$ denote the moduli stack of $n$-pointed curves of genus $g$ over $K$. For $x_n \in Y(K)$, we have a short exact sequence
0217 | \[
0218 | 1\to \pi _1 (Y_{\overline{K}},x)\to \pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,n,K},[(X,x_1 ,\ldots ,x_n )]) \to \pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,n-1,K},[(X,x_1 ,\ldots ,x_{n-1})]) \to 1,
0219 | \]
0220 | (see e.g. Nakamura--Tsunogai \cite{nakamura1993some}). This induces an outer action of \\
0221 | $\pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,n-1,K},[(X,x_1 ,\ldots ,x_{n-1})])$ on $\pi _1 ^{\et } (Y_{\overline{K}},x_n )$, which induces an outer action on the Malcev completion of $\pi _1 ^{\et }(Y_{\overline{K}},x_n )$, and hence an action on the graded pieces $\gr _i (U_i (Y)(x)$. When $n=1$ or $2$, the action of $\pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,n-1,K},[(X,x_1 ,\ldots ,x_{n-1})])$ on $U_1 (Y)=H_1 ^{\et } (X_{\overline{K}},\Q _p )$ has Zariski dense image in $\mathrm{GSp} (U_1 (X))$. The action of $G_K$ on $\gr _i (U_i (Y))$ factors through the action of $\pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,0,K},X)$ via the morphism
0222 | \begin{equation}\label{moduli_stack}
0223 | \Gal (\overline{K}|K)\to \pi _1 (\mathcal{M}_{g,n-1,K},[(X,x_1 ,\ldots ,x_{n-1})])
0224 | \end{equation}
0225 | induced by the morphism $\spec (K)\to \mathcal{M}_{g,n-1,K}$ induced by $[(X,(x_i ))]$.
